<article class="env-lemma" id="048O">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/048O">Lemma <span data-tag="048O">83.5.2</span>.</a> Let $B \to S$ as in Section <a href="/tag/048C" data-tag="048C">83.2</a>. Let $j : R \to U \times _ B U$ be a pre-equivalence relation of algebraic spaces over $B$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  O_ u = \{ u' \in |U| \text{ such that } \exists r \in |R|, \  s(r) = u, \  t(r) = u'\} .  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By the aforementioned Groupoids in Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/043F" data-tag="043F">78.4.4</a> we see that the orbits $O_ u$ as defined in the lemma give a disjoint union decomposition of $|U|$. Thus we see they are equal to the orbits as defined in Definition <a href="/tag/048N" data-tag="048N">83.5.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>